  "notes": "Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering. Software Engineering specialization (bulletin 2026-2027). Major = 45 cr with at least 26 cr at 300-level or above (this plan: 30 cr at 300+). Luddy degree requirements: Diversity in the U.S. (3 cr), Intensive Writing (3 cr), 12 cr Natural Science (AST/BIOL/CHEM/EAS/PHYS, non-Luddy, GenEd-approved), plus IU Common Ground. MATH-M 211 also satisfies the Common Ground Mathematical Modeling foundation; the 12 cr Natural Science satisfies the Common Ground N&M breadth. General electives may be used toward a minor or certificate (max 3 minors). C- or higher required in major courses; 2.0 major GPA. Prerequisite chains follow the official bulletin course descriptions. See the IU bulletin for official prerequisites.",
